# Local database credentials. `.env*` also covers .env.local, which the Vercel
# CLI writes with real connection strings on every `env pull`.
.env
.env*
# Re-stated after the wildcard above: the negation has to come last to win, and
# this file is the only record of which variables a deployment needs.
!.env.example

# Playwright MCP scratch output: console logs and page snapshots written during
# browser verification. Evidence for one session, not a record worth keeping.
.playwright-mcp/

# Screenshots taken while verifying a screen by hand. Name them and move them
# into docs/ if one is ever worth keeping; the root is not a scrapbook.
/seeded-*.png

# Browser accessibility-tree snapshots. The MCP tool writes these under
# .playwright-mcp/, but a verification run can be told to put one anywhere —
# one reached a commit as `audit-feed.yml`. Snapshots are evidence for a
# session, not a record; name and move one into docs/ if it is ever worth
# keeping.
/*-feed.yml
/page-*.yml
/console-*.log

# Raw doc-tool exports of the v2 specification, dropped at the repo root. The
# specs themselves live in docs/spec-v2/ as markdown and ARE tracked; these are
# the intermediate exports they came from. Excluded pending a decision rather
# than decided against — delete these three lines to track them.
/*.cd
